<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beatrice I, Countess of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1143–<a href="/years/1184">1184</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Beatrice I was countess of the Free County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> from 1148, the only child of Count Renaud III. Her marriage in 1156 to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> tied Burgundy to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>, and she was crowned empress in 1167 and queen of Burgundy in 1178. Her children included the emperor Henry VI and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i-duke-of-bavaria">Otto I</a>, Count of Burgundy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beatrice-i-countess-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Beatrice I, Countess of Burgundy" width="210" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BeatrixBarbarossy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
